commit ad5f1d36cb628b362ef7a3a7de66a0ce415db756
Author: InnoPeak <global_ai@innopeaktech.com>
Date:   Wed May 20 00:44:25 2026 -0700

    feat(tauri-capability-allowlist): add db capability file + runtime window allow-list
    
    Why
    - G2.5 requires the desktop crate to (a) document every JS-callable
      command's allowed windows in a capability file and (b) enforce that
      allow-list at runtime so a mis-attached capability cannot widen the
      surface silently. Database commands landed in G2.2 without a
      dedicated capability file or runtime check, leaving `db_*` reachable
      from any window that happened to have `core:default`.
    
    What
    - Add `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/plugin-data-database.json`
      scoped to `main`, `control`, `grid_*`, `account`, `console`. Widget /
      pet / ai-cube windows are explicitly excluded.
    - Add defence-in-depth `DATABASE_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` runtime check in
      `commands/database.rs` (returns `E3004 SyncCapabilityDenied` on bad
      origin). Mirrors the existing `CRYPTO_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` pattern.
    - 2 new cargo tests cover the admit (main / control / account /
      console / `grid_*` prefix) and reject (widget / pet / ai-cube /
      unknown) paths.
    - Add `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md` recording the full
      audit table: windows ↔ commands ↔ capability file ↔ runtime allow-
      list.
    - Update `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §6.1 and §7 with the new
      capability file and audit pointer; document the two-layer invariant.
    - Create `packages/tauri-capability-allowlist/docs/dev_log.md` and
      promote G2 manifest row #6 to READY_TO_SHIP.
    
    Scope
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/ (new file + audit doc),
      commands/database.rs (window-origin checks + tests),
      packages/tauri-capability-allowlist/docs/,
      docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md, G2 manifest, autorun.
    
    Risk
    - Low. New runtime check is purely additive; legitimate callers
      (main / control / grid_* / account / console) keep their access.
      MAS signed-runtime smoke remains deferred.
    
    Docs
    - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md,
      apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md,
      packages/tauri-capability-allowlist/docs/dev_log.md, G2 manifest,
      autorun.
    
    Tests
    - cargo check --features crypto : PASS
    - cargo check (default) : PASS
    - cargo test --features crypto database:: : 9 tests PASS
    - pnpm --filter desktop build : PASS
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

